# Defensive .gitignore for a git repo whose root is $HOME.
#
# Because the repo root is the home directory, a bare `git add -A` would
# otherwise stage credentials, SSH keys, WordPress configs, and SQL dumps
# containing customer data. Strategy: ignore everything, then re-allow only
# the specific paths that are actually tracked work.

*

# --- Re-allow only what is genuinely tracked ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!Sites/
!Sites/purple bee systems/
!Sites/purple bee systems/.agents/
!Sites/purple bee systems/.agents/**

# --- Hard denials. Keep these last so nothing above can re-expose them. ---

# Credentials, keys, agent state
.ssh/
.gnupg/
.aws/
.config/
.buzz/
.claude/
.codex/
.goose/
Library/
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc

# Key and cert material anywhere
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keychain
*_rsa
*_ed25519
id_*

# Application secrets anywhere
**/wp-config.php
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/claude_desktop_config.json
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
**/token.json
**/*token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/service-account*.json

# Database dumps — these carry live customer data
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*.dump
